    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="4493a684-1f9d-5708-8579-7d91f88296dd" activityNameId="6b3dbcd2-4dab-5269-a494-e6d217b4f670" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Disposal, ventilation unit 13000 m3/h, w. cross plate heat excanger</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Disposal, ventilation unit 13000 m3/h, w. cross plate heat excanger
Disposal of a ventilation unit (air handling unit) with 13000 m3/h nominal air flow rate (at 2 m/s air speed in cross section of air filter or heat exchanger), component weight: 3275 kg, total weight: 3667 kg/Unit, including average components for controls, inverter and electric control cabinet, material for 20 filter replacements (once a year for 20 years lifetime). The air handling unit includes a frame construction, two radial belt drive fans, two multi-leaf damper, heat recovery with aluminium plate heat exchanger, heating elements, expansion plenum and empty section in supply and extract air. No cooling elements, humidifier, air-mixing plenum and silencer included. The frame construction made of aluminium-profiles, casing made of hot-dip galvanized and powder coated steel sheets insulated with polyurethane foam.;
UUID: 9ee0e60b-c3ac-4c86-b0b6-2dbc40c04c44
Transport to dismantling facilities, machines for handling in sorting plant, electricity demand for sorting plant, final disposal of waste material. Cut-off to recycling for metals.
Location: Specific to the technology mix encountered in sorting plants in Switzerland.
Technology: Disposal to a sorting plant assumed. Metal pieces, copper in cables and electronic devices are recycled, plastic parts are incinerated, inert wastes (e.g. rock wool) are landfilled.
Time period: Amount of material investigated in 2013. Disposal technology mix as used in late 1990ies
Production volume: na
Sampling: Waste-specific calculation based on production input data 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_9ee0e60b-c3ac-4c86-b0b6-2dbc40c04c44.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
